WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.251 --> 00:00:02.084
(baby talks)

00:00:02.084 --> 00:00:04.210
- Yeah, okay. Good job!

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:05.990
Yeah, good job. Well done.

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:08.230
Hi, everyone. My name is Kristen.

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:10.860
I have an 11 month old son named Wyatt

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.853
and I'm really excited
because we're going to

00:00:12.853 --> 00:00:14.574
teach him sign language for a week.

00:00:14.574 --> 00:00:15.864
(gasps)

00:00:15.864 --> 00:00:17.410
(laughs)

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:19.590
Wyatt seems to get frustrated easily

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:21.160
when he can't communicate with us.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.510
- Outside of him pointing at things,

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.450
I think it's really good to be able to

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.783
have actual words and description.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.733
Only good can come from it.

00:00:28.898 --> 00:00:32.260
- If I were going to bet,
I would say he'll learn

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.493
at least three signs throughout the week.

00:00:34.872 --> 00:00:36.770
- I don't think he'll learn in a week, no.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.587
(laughs)

00:00:38.587 --> 00:00:40.687
I don't think anyone will learn in a week.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.143
- Who's teaching it to him?
- We all are.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.730
- You can tell the way he's pointing,

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.580
he repeats as much as he
can, so I think he is just

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.110
very anxious to have a way
to communicate with us,

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:54.560
so I think it's gonna be fun.

00:00:58.555 --> 00:01:00.055
- Mmm. Okay, wait.

00:01:01.079 --> 00:01:03.240
You do it. More. More, like this.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.563
Look, more. You do it. More.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.023
Do you want more food?
Like this. More, more.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.020
Every kid is so different
that you kind of have

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.420
to tailor the words that you're teaching

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.733
to them to what makes sense for them.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.273
Look, Wyatt. Do you want more?

00:01:21.942 --> 00:01:24.783
Yeah! Good job!

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.933
I had to go this morning
to a meeting with a client,

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:31.890
so we had our nanny here and I showed her

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.490
some of the signs we were doing.

00:01:34.336 --> 00:01:35.638
(laughs)

00:01:35.638 --> 00:01:38.270
He's like, "But mom, this
is so much more effective."

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:42.300
A busy life and an
on-the-go life does make it

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.150
difficult to get this done in a week.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.660
And it feels like I'm being unfair to him

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:51.350
if I'm not giving it
110% or if my husband's

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:53.510
not or whoever else is around him.

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:56.040
I'm finding that it's actually easier

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:59.080
not to so much focus on specific words,

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:01.920
but instead try and find times where

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.160
there are good, teachable moments.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.803
And he's sitting down and eating.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.470
He's looking at me,
he's making eye contact.

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:11.077
It's almost like we're
bartering, where I'm like,

00:02:11.077 --> 00:02:13.380
"okay, try and do more,"
and he gets something.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.780
When we're doing things like
trying to play with him,

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:20.333
I keep trying to say
ball or book or walker.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:24.480
It's a little more
difficult because it's hard

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.580
to be playing with him
while using my hands.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.790
And he's playing with the actual object

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:31.790
and it's not like--I don't wanna
just take it away from him.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:33.853
- Ball? Ball.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:35.950
Good.
(baby exclaims)

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:38.283
- Yeah!
(laughs)

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.360
He's kind of already
saying some of the words,

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.730
which makes it a little tricky.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:45.370
So it makes it difficult to
basically try and convince

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:47.017
him to use sign language when he's like,

00:02:47.017 --> 00:02:48.610
"hey mom, I can say this word."

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:50.723
Show mama your car. Your car.

00:02:51.949 --> 00:02:53.863
Can you do it? Car.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.310
- Still a good possibility, because

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:58.610
it's not like he's
speaking in full sentences.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.573
- So, we'll see.

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:03.047
We're not supposed to
let him play with toys

00:03:03.047 --> 00:03:06.363
while he eats breakfast or any meal.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.613
But I think he's not feeling great today.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:12.790
He has a little bit of a cough.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:15.983
So I'm softie and I'm giving in.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:20.613
But I will say it makes it
incredibly difficult to sign.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.163
(baby speaks)
- Yeah.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:25.610
I've found that any distractions

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:31.363
when signing make it (gasps)
basically impossible.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:35.303
Wyatt, do you want more?
More? Look, more food? More.

00:03:37.429 --> 00:03:38.262
Oh! (laughs)

00:03:38.262 --> 00:03:42.100
I try and teach him and
if he doesn't get it

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.233
but like is the middle of eating,

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.040
I know that he wants more
food and I just feel like

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.950
a bad mom if I'm just
not giving it to him.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.020
So, I don't know. I think that

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:53.660
that obviously makes it difficult that

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:58.593
I'm too easy on him but, oh well.

00:03:58.749 --> 00:04:03.063
Day four and the struggle is real.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:05.160
I have to be honest, sign language is

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.973
kind of taking a backseat today.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.340
You know, mom life, what can you do?

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:12.120
You can't plan for so much. I feel like

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:13.850
I can plan for like half hour increments,

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:15.860
basically, and then you
just have to be flexible.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:18.510
I think him not feeling great, you know,

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:21.143
made me want to, again, keep him happy.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:25.910
And so day four did not go as planned.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.813
But there's always day five, right?

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:36.160
Yeah, okay. Good job!
Yeah, good job, all done.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.823
He did start to somewhat sign all done.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.710
I think the reason is, with
all the other signs so far,

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:45.130
he's either able to say
the word or he knows,

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:46.530
like, for example, with more,

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:48.230
he can pick up his own food and eat more

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:50.280
or he know that we'll give him more food.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:52.587
When he's done eating, I think he like,

00:04:52.587 --> 00:04:55.367
"I am done eating, get this away from me."

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:00.840
Overall, we still got one
word, and that is like amazing.

00:05:01.922 --> 00:05:06.730
Day six. Wyatt went to his
grandparents' house today.

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:08.603
He did not learn sign language,

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.523
but he did have a great time.

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:12.417
I think, in the beginning
of the week I was like,

00:05:12.417 --> 00:05:14.770
"Oh, he really wants to
communicate and he gets

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:16.638
frustrated and this will
help us communicate."

00:05:16.638 --> 00:05:19.290
And by the end of the
week, I've kind of realized

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.131
we're actually really
great at communicating.

00:05:21.131 --> 00:05:22.980
- Ball!
- That's right, that's a ball.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:26.550
Good job. This experience has been awesome

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:30.530
in terms of realizing how
close we are and how much

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.540
we understand each other and I love that.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:35.023
Final day. What to you think, Wy?

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:40.883
I think so, too. You had fun?

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:45.010
We just found what formula
works best for Wyatt.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:46.070
And I think that's a great point.

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:48.140
I think if any lesson
that we learned from this,

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:52.133
it's that every kid is so
different, as I've often said.

00:05:52.155 --> 00:05:54.900
And you need to communicate with your kid

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:56.440
the way that works best for them.

00:05:56.440 --> 00:06:00.583
But clearly we have someone
here who likes to talk.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:01.893
Yeah.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:03.630
Can I have a kiss?

00:06:03.821 --> 00:06:05.321
Can I have a kiss?

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:07.566
Aww, mwah.

